mlx-vlm 0.4.4: cast mx.array scalars to int before using them as counts.

Carried from upstream Blaizzy/mlx-vlm commit 1249c7db09921714b43e056b149f9d762eec07d3
("Fix instances of mx.arrays being used as integers which will break in the next MLX
release", Lucas Newman, 2026-08-20; first released in mlx-vlm 0.6.16), re-diffed against the
0.4.4 wheel so it applies at exact offsets. The upstream commit's twelfth file,
minimax_h3/references.py, does not exist in 0.4.4. Applied by python/parts.nix in postInstall
because wheel sources are never unpacked. Drop it when mlx-vlm is bumped to >= 0.6.16.

diff a/mlx_vlm/models/aya_vision/vision.py b/mlx_vlm/models/aya_vision/vision.py
--- a/mlx_vlm/models/aya_vision/vision.py
+++ b/mlx_vlm/models/aya_vision/vision.py
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@
 
         for i in range(batch_size):
             # (1, dim, height, width) -> (1, dim, target_height, target_width)
-            height, width = spatial_shapes[i]
+            height, width = spatial_shapes[i].tolist()
             # Then upsample width dimension
             resized_embeddings = resize_bilinear(
                 positional_embeddings,
diff a/mlx_vlm/models/dots_ocr/vision.py b/mlx_vlm/models/dots_ocr/vision.py
--- a/mlx_vlm/models/dots_ocr/vision.py
+++ b/mlx_vlm/models/dots_ocr/vision.py
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@
         cu_seqlens = []
         for i in range(grid_thw.shape[0]):
             seq_len = grid_thw[i, 1] * grid_thw[i, 2]
-            cu_seqlens.append(mx.repeat(seq_len, grid_thw[i, 0]))
+            cu_seqlens.append(mx.repeat(seq_len, int(grid_thw[i, 0])))
         cu_seqlens = mx.concatenate(cu_seqlens).astype(mx.int32)
         cu_seqlens = mx.cumsum(cu_seqlens, axis=0)
         cu_seqlens = mx.pad(cu_seqlens, (1, 0), constant_values=0)
